{"seq":4,"slug":"writing-foundations","title":"写作基础功","stage":"DONE","category":"writing","chapterCount":5,"docCount":20,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations","rating":{"composite":3.97,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4.4,"coverage":4,"positioning":4.5,"strategic":3},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.59,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":3.25}},"introMarkdown":"# 写作基础功 简介\n\n写作能力的高低，最终取决于基本功是否扎实。许多写作者在追求文采飞扬或谋篇布局的同时，忽略了用词是否精准、句式是否通顺、标点是否规范这些看似微小却至关重要的基础问题。就像一座建筑的地基决定了它能承载多高的楼层，写作的基础功决定了你能驾驭多复杂的表达。一篇文章即使立意再高远、结构再精巧，如果遣词造句漏洞百出，读者的信任感和阅读体验也会大打折扣。\n\n本知识库面向所有希望系统性夯实写作基本功的写作者，无论你是刚刚起步的写作新手，还是已有一定经验但感到表达能力遇到瓶颈的中级写作者。如果你发现自己写出来的文字总是\"差一点感觉\"，或者在修改时不知道该从哪里改起，这里将为你提供清晰的自查框架和系统的提升路径。\n\n全书共分五个章节，从最小的语言单位逐步扩展到整篇文章的组织：\n\n第一章**词汇与措辞**聚焦写作中最基本的单元——词语。你将学习如何在相近词语中选择最精准的那一个，理解词语的感情色彩和语域差异，掌握有效扩充写作词汇的方法，并识别常见的措辞误用，从根源上提升表达的准确性。\n\n第二章**语法与句式**从句子层面入手，帮助你掌握不同句式的构造与表达效果。从基本的句子结构到从句与短语的灵活运用，从平行结构的对称美感到常见语法陷阱的规避，这一章将让你的句子既正确又富有表现力。\n\n第三章**标点与格式**关注那些容易被忽视却直接影响阅读体验的细节。正确的标点使用能让句意清晰无歧义，规范的段落格式让读者的眼睛轻松导航，合理的文档版式提升整体的专业感，而引用与参考的规范则体现写作者的严谨态度。\n\n第四章**段落与连贯**将视角从句子提升到段落。你将学习如何写出有力的主题句、如何让段落内部形成逻辑上的衔接与连贯、如何运用过渡技巧让段落之间自然流转，以及不同功能的段落应当采用怎样的展开模式。\n\n第五章**提纲与结构**站在整篇文章的高度，帮助你在动笔之前就规划好全文的骨架。从提纲的设计方法到常见的结构模型，从信息层级的合理安排到以读者为中心的结构策略，这一章将让你写出的每一篇文章都有清晰的逻辑脉络。\n\n建议按照章节顺序依次学习，因为每一章的内容都建立在前一章的基础之上——先能精准用词，再能造出好句，进而组织好段落，最终统筹全篇。如果你已有一定基础，也可以根据自己的薄弱环节有针对性地选择章节深入研读。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"vocabulary-and-diction","title":"词汇与措辞","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/vocabulary-and-diction","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"word-choice-precision","title":"精准选词","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/vocabulary-and-diction/word-choice-precision"},{"seq":2,"slug":"connotation-and-register","title":"词语内涵与语域","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/vocabulary-and-diction/connotation-and-register"},{"seq":3,"slug":"vocabulary-expansion","title":"词汇扩展策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/vocabulary-and-diction/vocabulary-expansion"},{"seq":4,"slug":"common-diction-errors","title":"常见用词错误","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/vocabulary-and-diction/common-diction-errors"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"grammar-and-sentences","title":"语法与句式","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/grammar-and-sentences","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"sentence-structure-mastery","title":"句式掌握","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/grammar-and-sentences/sentence-structure-mastery"},{"seq":2,"slug":"clause-and-phrase","title":"从句与短语","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/grammar-and-sentences/clause-and-phrase"},{"seq":3,"slug":"parallelism-and-balance","title":"排比与平衡","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/grammar-and-sentences/parallelism-and-balance"},{"seq":4,"slug":"common-grammar-pitfalls","title":"常见语法陷阱","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/grammar-and-sentences/common-grammar-pitfalls"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"punctuation-and-format","title":"标点与格式","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/punctuation-and-format","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"punctuation-rules","title":"标点规则","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/punctuation-and-format/punctuation-rules"},{"seq":2,"slug":"paragraph-formatting","title":"段落排版","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/punctuation-and-format/paragraph-formatting"},{"seq":3,"slug":"document-layout","title":"文档版式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/punctuation-and-format/document-layout"},{"seq":4,"slug":"citation-and-references","title":"引用与参考文献","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/punctuation-and-format/citation-and-references"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"paragraph-and-coherence","title":"段落与连贯","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/paragraph-and-coherence","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"topic-sentences","title":"主题句","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/paragraph-and-coherence/topic-sentences"},{"seq":2,"slug":"coherence-and-cohesion","title":"连贯与衔接","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/paragraph-and-coherence/coherence-and-cohesion"},{"seq":3,"slug":"transition-techniques","title":"过渡技巧","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/paragraph-and-coherence/transition-techniques"},{"seq":4,"slug":"paragraph-patterns","title":"段落模式","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/paragraph-and-coherence/paragraph-patterns"}]},{"seq":5,"slug":"outline-and-structure","title":"提纲与结构","docCount":4,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/outline-and-structure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"outline-design-methods","title":"提纲设计方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/outline-and-structure/outline-design-methods"},{"seq":2,"slug":"structural-models","title":"结构模型","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/outline-and-structure/structural-models"},{"seq":3,"slug":"information-hierarchy","title":"信息层级","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/outline-and-structure/information-hierarchy"},{"seq":4,"slug":"reader-oriented-structure","title":"读者导向结构","url":"/l-doc-books/h/writing/writing-foundations/outline-and-structure/reader-oriented-structure"}]}]}